    <string name="dlg_decoy">DECOY PASSWORD</string>
    <!-- docs/DECOY-ACCOUNT.md §3: replacing may say so plainly ONCE THE DIALOG IS OPEN, because
         only the account that owns the decoy can get here and anyone who compelled that account
         has already won. The row itself stays identical everywhere. -->
    <string name="dlg_decoy_replace_msg">this replaces the decoy this account already has. its messages and its username go with it, and the new password is the only one that will open it.</string>
    <string name="btn_decoy_replace">REPLACE</string>
    <string name="decoy_status_replaced">✓ decoy replaced</string>
    <string name="dlg_decoy_msg">a second, real account with its own username, contacts and history. entering its password at unlock opens it instead of this one, and nothing in the app ever shows that it exists.\n\nit protects against someone at the scene who can make you unlock once. it does not defeat a lab that knows this feature exists.</string>
